§ `ss 7, 56, 58, 61, 62 -- applying and being assessed`

-- c097: Chloe, 82, with difficulty with daily living (ASSUMED), may apply and can be found eligible; s 58(c) does not reach her.
#ASSERT `Do I have care needs` TRUE FALSE

#ASSERT NOT (`May I apply for access to funded aged care services` TRUE)

#ASSERT `Am I old enough to be assessed for aged care` 50 TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I old enough to be assessed for aged care` 49 TRUE TRUE)

#ASSERT `Can I be found eligible for an aged care needs assessment` 82 FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Can I be found eligible for an aged care needs assessment` 82 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Can I be found eligible for an aged care needs assessment` 55 TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE)

#ASSERT NOT (`Will my aged care needs assessment go ahead` TRUE TRUE)

§ `ss 8, 10, 65-68 -- Support at Home or residential care, and what can be approved`

-- c097: Chloe at home in Mandurah can get home support there; her approval names service types (s 65(2)(b)).
#ASSERT `Which kind of care can be delivered where I am` `my own home` FALSE EQUALS `home support, assistive technology or home modifications`
#ASSERT `Which kind of care can be delivered where I am` `an approved residential care home` FALSE EQUALS `residential care`

#ASSERT NOT (`Is the place a home or community setting` `my own home` TRUE)

-- c097: Chloe's impairment (ASSUMED) and a s 67(1)(b) purpose, or a medical service for sickness, let home support be approved.
#ASSERT `Can home support services of this type be approved for me` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Can home support services of this type be approved for me` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `Can home support services of this type be approved for me` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE

#ASSERT NOT (`Can residential care be approved for me` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE)

#ASSERT `Will my approval be limited to particular service types` `home support` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Will my approval be limited to particular service types` `residential care` FALSE)

§ `ss 84, 86(5), 9(2), 92A -- priority, place, and getting the service`

#ASSERT `Must I be given a priority category` `home support` `ongoing` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Must I be given a priority category` `home support` `ongoing` TRUE)
#ASSERT `Must I be given a priority category` `home modifications` `short-term` FALSE

#ASSERT `What priority category must I be given for residential care` `low` FALSE TRUE EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `What priority category must I be given for residential care` `low` FALSE FALSE EQUALS 3

-- c097: where Chloe is on the way into her Support at Home package.
#ASSERT `What am I still waiting for` `Chloe in June 2085, her provider started in time` EQUALS `nothing -- I can get the service`
#ASSERT `What am I still waiting for` `Chloe approved and prioritised, no place yet` EQUALS `a place to be allocated`
#ASSERT `What am I still waiting for` `Chloe with a place, the start day outside the rules' period` EQUALS `a provider to start my services within the period the rules allow`
#ASSERT `What am I still waiting for` `Chloe, the rules excusing prioritisation and a place` EQUALS `nothing -- I can get the service`

#ASSERT `Can I get funded home support services now` `Chloe in June 2085, her provider started in time`

#ASSERT NOT (`Can my access approval start from my first service day` 6 5 TRUE)

§ `ss 72, 73 and the notices`

#ASSERT NOT (`May I ask for it to be revoked` `my eligibility determination` 82 TRUE)
#ASSERT `May I ask for it to be revoked` `my access approval` 82 TRUE

#ASSERT `Within how many days must I be told` `my application to have my residential contributions taken as zero` EQUALS 28

§ `s 273 -- what Chloe contributes at home`

-- c097: two hours' cleaning at a base price of 80 and a provider price of 90: 50% of 2 x 80 = 80. Personal care: 17.5% of
-- 2 x 95 = 33.25. A cost-based service at 50% of 300 = 150. Rates and prices HYPOTHETICAL.
#ASSERT `What is my individual contribution for the service` `home support` `Chloe's cleaning, two hours at everyday living 50%` FALSE EQUALS 80
#ASSERT `What is my individual contribution for the service` `home support` `Chloe's cleaning with a 10 dollar fee reduction supplement` FALSE EQUALS 70
#ASSERT `What is my individual contribution for the service` `home support` `Chloe's personal care, two hours at independence 17.5%` FALSE EQUALS 33.25
#ASSERT `What is my individual contribution for the service` `home support` `a cost-based service at 50% costing 300` FALSE EQUALS 150

#ASSERT `What is my individual contribution for the service` `home support` `Chloe's cleaning, two hours at everyday living 50%` TRUE EQUALS 0

#ASSERT `Has the lifetime cap ended what I contribute` 61000 5000 0 65000

#ASSERT NOT (`Can my provider make me pay my contribution yet` FALSE)

§ `s 319 -- the daily means tested amount`

-- Hypothetical thresholds chosen so each band divides by 364. Income 45000: 3640 + 1820 = 5460 / 364 = 15.
#ASSERT `What is my per day income tested amount` 30728 `the hypothetical rules numbers` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `What is my per day income tested amount` 45000 `the hypothetical rules numbers` EQUALS 15
#ASSERT `What is my per day income tested amount` 50728 `the hypothetical rules numbers` EQUALS 16

-- Assets 120000: 17.5% of 20800 = 3640, plus 7.8% of 14000 = 1092; 4732 / 364 = 13.
#ASSERT `What is my per day asset tested amount` 120000 `the hypothetical rules numbers` EQUALS 13
#ASSERT `What is my per day asset tested amount` 164000 `the hypothetical rules numbers` EQUALS 16

#ASSERT `What is my daily means tested amount` 45000 120000 `the hypothetical rules numbers` EQUALS 28

#ASSERT `What is my asset free area` 30000 FALSE 0 EQUALS 67500

§ `ss 276-282 -- what I would contribute in a residential care home`

-- 85% of a HYPOTHETICAL 71.81 a day is 61.0385, rounded down to 61.03.
#ASSERT `What is my basic daily fee` 71.81 FALSE 0 EQUALS 61.03

#ASSERT `What is my hotelling contribution` `a resident with 80 a day` EQUALS 10
#ASSERT `What is my hotelling contribution` `a resident with 150 a day` EQUALS 20
#ASSERT `What is my hotelling contribution` `a resident with means not disclosed` EQUALS 20

#ASSERT `What is my non-clinical care contribution` `a resident with 80 a day` FALSE FALSE EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `What is my non-clinical care contribution` `a resident with 150 a day` FALSE FALSE EQUALS 60
#ASSERT `What is my non-clinical care contribution` `a resident with means not disclosed` FALSE FALSE EQUALS 100

#ASSERT `What is the most my resident contribution can be for a day` 61.03 0 `a resident with 150 a day` FALSE FALSE EQUALS 141.03

#ASSERT `On how many days can I be charged a pre-entry fee` 20 EQUALS 7

#ASSERT `May I be charged a bed reservation fee` TRUE FALSE 52

§ `ss 296, 298, 301, 305 -- paying for the room`

#ASSERT `What can I be charged for my room` TRUE 28 70 FALSE EQUALS `an accommodation contribution`
#ASSERT `What can I be charged for my room` FALSE 0 70 FALSE EQUALS `an accommodation payment`

#ASSERT `What is the most my daily accommodation contribution can be` 70 80 90 EQUALS 70

#ASSERT NOT (`May I be charged interest on an overdue daily payment` TRUE TRUE 9 8)

-- 2.25 x 30120 = 67770, to the nearest 500 = 68000; 2.25 x 30100 = 67725 rounds to 67500.
#ASSERT `What is my minimum permissible asset value` 30120 0 EQUALS 68000
#ASSERT `What is my minimum permissible asset value` 30100 0 EQUALS 67500

#ASSERT NOT (`May my provider accept this refundable deposit` TRUE 10 50000 67500)

§ `ss 23, 24, 358 -- the Statement of Rights`

-- c097: Chloe, seeking access, has the Statement of Rights; she can complain, not sue.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to the Statement of Rights` TRUE

#ASSERT `Does the Statement of Rights give me this right` `to records and information about my rights, my services and their costs`
#ASSERT NOT (`Does the Statement of Rights give me this right` `to choose among services I have not been approved to access`)

#ASSERT `Where can I take a breach of my rights` TRUE EQUALS `the Complaints Commissioner`

